    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "8362ddaf-1b91-3c4a-b930-7b1e4caea8a6",
                "word": "formful",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d4840474-768f-4cd1-b9d3-1b0737b17fdc",
                        "entry_id": "8362ddaf-1b91-3c4a-b930-7b1e4caea8a6",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more formful"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "98bb8afb-e0f4-420d-9305-c1f8596742c8",
                        "entry_id": "8362ddaf-1b91-3c4a-b930-7b1e4caea8a6",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most formful"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "330ff421-45f3-352e-a2b8-f6ab297adffb",
                        "entry_id": "8362ddaf-1b91-3c4a-b930-7b1e4caea8a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "creative; imaginative;"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b37a1346-0fc9-46d2-89b7-cd03e49dfe6e",
                                "sense_id": "330ff421-45f3-352e-a2b8-f6ab297adffb",
                                "text": "As fleets the vision o'er the formful brain"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8448c94-6024-4edd-bbfe-28b771a3b88c",
                                "sense_id": "330ff421-45f3-352e-a2b8-f6ab297adffb",
                                "text": "Fearless, with face oblique, her formful hand Flies o'er the ivory Plain, with stretch'd command; Plunges, with bold neglect, amidst the keys, And sweeps the sounding range with magic east."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "24b3e1d8-7766-30e7-9f61-99a0346759f1",
                        "entry_id": "8362ddaf-1b91-3c4a-b930-7b1e4caea8a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not formless; having a form; substantive."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "90d41dcc-87d4-44c7-860a-199dbfad5e15",
                                "sense_id": "24b3e1d8-7766-30e7-9f61-99a0346759f1",
                                "text": "Creation is at root a process of rendering formful and substantial (\"filled\") what was originally amorphous and empty, of establishing domains and their appropriate populace."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0e85976-2c3c-48af-a346-60808a7ad192",
                                "sense_id": "24b3e1d8-7766-30e7-9f61-99a0346759f1",
                                "text": "How one can say that - God is only formful."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9609f389-e836-4c82-ac4d-5e3f698f62a1",
                                "sense_id": "24b3e1d8-7766-30e7-9f61-99a0346759f1",
                                "text": "Out of the formless the formful has come into being."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6086a2fa-e33c-39ae-8b74-cf3e0d8ed6ef",
                        "entry_id": "8362ddaf-1b91-3c4a-b930-7b1e4caea8a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Well formed; aesthetically pleasing and skillfully constructed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "af87f504-91d3-4ae4-8f06-2bc869f23b23",
                                "sense_id": "6086a2fa-e33c-39ae-8b74-cf3e0d8ed6ef",
                                "text": "Potters are craftworkers; that is, they use their hands to make objects for everyday use that need to have form and design as an integral part of their being. To be able to do this potters need a certain ability, not only of the hands (as most might think) but especially a capacity to see what is formful, beautiful, characteristic and so on."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a9187b9-d357-4cb6-b7ef-c317e20a4f05",
                                "sense_id": "6086a2fa-e33c-39ae-8b74-cf3e0d8ed6ef",
                                "text": "We are all often indignant, and sometimes witty about our indignations, but we do not thereby turn satirists. For it is not only the anger and the involvement, the idealism and the wit, but the manipulations of them, how they are turned to formful, organic use that constitute the satric art."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a22a7f7e-4b94-46e1-abc6-a1cc421654d4",
                                "sense_id": "6086a2fa-e33c-39ae-8b74-cf3e0d8ed6ef",
                                "text": "If we must guard against the notions of form, coherence or justifying too narrowly, in terms of what is generally praised as “harmony” and “balance,” we must equally avoid interpreting them so broadly that everything whatever is “formful” simply because it has parts in relation to one another."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d968a067-67d0-3f47-b6b5-2e93f6dbb277",
                        "entry_id": "8362ddaf-1b91-3c4a-b930-7b1e4caea8a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Exhibiting proper and skillful performance; well-executed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "35a99051-e6c7-4421-acb7-6046716dfa6c",
                                "sense_id": "d968a067-67d0-3f47-b6b5-2e93f6dbb277",
                                "text": "The number of winning favorites is one of the best indications of formful racing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48280a43-56c7-4ca4-b141-666cf7b81c85",
                                "sense_id": "d968a067-67d0-3f47-b6b5-2e93f6dbb277",
                                "text": "Pitchers: Grip, receiving signals on mound, working with a wind-up, working from stretch position, formful delivery and follow through, holding runner close, strategy, working on control by pitching through the strings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0356294e-d5b4-44d2-bed4-1fc9eb0de15b",
                                "sense_id": "d968a067-67d0-3f47-b6b5-2e93f6dbb277",
                                "text": "If your finish position is sound, balanced, and formful, then the mechanics necessary to give you that result had to occur!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "888644d9-7be3-3330-b2ac-12e553f2f8fd",
                "word": "formful",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2a25e098-0cd4-4020-b818-8176388ac8f1",
                        "entry_id": "888644d9-7be3-3330-b2ac-12e553f2f8fd",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "formfuls"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1a296e9b-5f51-3941-b0b3-92b56288d5aa",
                        "entry_id": "888644d9-7be3-3330-b2ac-12e553f2f8fd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The amount that makes up a form (any sense)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "95bdae9e-e2b7-47f5-a192-7234f4b74e51",
                                "sense_id": "1a296e9b-5f51-3941-b0b3-92b56288d5aa",
                                "text": "In order to keep themselves awake, each formful of people appoints a watchman — (and they take this office in turns each hour' throughout the night), — whose duty it is, with a small stick, if necessary, to give a smart rap to the poor exhausted creature who may be dozing off to sleep."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "faa72ef9-e288-4f67-b08d-3fa61aadfdba",
                                "sense_id": "1a296e9b-5f51-3941-b0b3-92b56288d5aa",
                                "text": "For this reason, it is important to score the center rod with marks at four-inch intervals to that Slip Form walls will progress upward uniformly, coinciding with the structure's various floor levels and window sill heights; that is, so that floors and sills will be level with layers of wall, dispensing with the need to cast half a formful of mortar to make up for any difference in levels of the various building components."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5acd7e2c-9ecb-49f4-95b3-3fac5feb271b",
                                "sense_id": "1a296e9b-5f51-3941-b0b3-92b56288d5aa",
                                "text": "This fits in with Hudson's (1966) observation that 'a knowledge of a boy's IQ is of little help if you are faced with a formful of clever boys' (p. 127), and with the idea that personality and motivational factors may well be more important than cognitive abilities in promoting real-life creativity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "53e7d27d-350f-44af-97f8-7bf144fd9e47",
                                "sense_id": "1a296e9b-5f51-3941-b0b3-92b56288d5aa",
                                "text": "Pausing under a tree, picking and sniffing through the Gravensteins, yellow skins splashed with magenta drip, firm formfuls of breathtaking smells, a dull thud draws me to the next."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
